oo up 6, Braun Research shows Scott up 10", "Janoo outraised Scott in September, signaling an energized Democratic challenge", "Prediction markets still price Scott as a clear favorite (roughly 24-35% for Janoo)"], "rationale": "The polling average puts Scott ahead by about three points, but the two most recent surveys disagree sharply, with UNH showing Janoo ahead and Braun Research showing a ten-point Scott lead. Expert ratings mostly call the race Solid or Likely R, markets favor Scott, and his incumbency in a Democratic-leaning state has historically proven durable, so a narrow Republican edge with wide uncertainty is the reasonable landing point.", "watch": "Whether subsequent polling confirms the UNH result showing Janoo ahead or reverts to the pattern of double-digit Scott leads.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Phil Scott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont's governor race pits four-term Republican incumbent Phil Scott against Democrat Amanda Janoo in a state that leans heavily Democratic at the presidential level but has repeatedly reelected Scott by wide margins. The race has tightened unusually: a late-September UNH poll shows Janoo ahead 49-43, while a Braun Research survey from the same period gives Scott a ten-point lead, and earlier summer polls had him up double digits. Janoo also outraised Scott in September, and headlines describe the contest as competitive.\n\nStill, most expert raters call the race Solid or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Janoo roughly a one-in-four to one-in-three chance. The forecast lands on a narrow Scott lead with elevated uncertainty, reflecting the conflict between his incumbency advantage and genuine signs of a contested race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26